# Home Assistant & Grafana Premium Dashboard Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the steps to establish a long-term data pipeline using InfluxDB v2 and Grafana, and to design a premium, mobile-optimized Home Assistant dashboard for your phone and tablet.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **InfluxDB v2 Token**: I'll be generating a new administration token to allow Home Assistant to write data.
> **Mushroom Cards**: The "Premium" UI will rely on the `Mushroom` card system. If it's not already installed via HACS, I will do so as part of the execution.
> **Dashboard Scope**: We'll start with your environmental sensors (Mi Temp) and the Dreame vacuum, keeping the initial setup "small and effective" as requested.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. InfluxDB v2 Pipeline [Backend]
- **Create Bucket**: Initialize a `homeassistant` bucket in InfluxDB to store historical data.
- **Access Token**: Generate a secure token for Home Assistant authentication.
- **HA Configuration**: Modify `configuration.yaml` to enable the InfluxDB integration with precision logging for your sensors.

### 2. Premium Mobile Dashboard [Home Assistant]
#### [NEW] [mobile_dashboard.yaml](file:///DATA/AppData/homeassistant/config/ui-lovelace-mobile.yaml)
- **Concept**: A minimalist, "Glassmorphism" or "Mushroom" style dashboard.
- **Features**:
  - **Quick Actions**: Top-level buttons for common tasks (Start Vacuum, All Lights Off).
  - **Environment Glance**: Large, clear readouts for temperature and humidity from the Mi Temp sensor.
  - **Cleaning Center**: Dedicated section for "Bella" (Dreame Vacuum) status and controls.
  - **Responsive Layout**: Optimized for both handheld phones and larger tablet screens.

### 3. Grafana Analytics [Visualization]
- **Data Source**: Connect Grafana to the new InfluxDB bucket.
- **Dashboards**:
  - **Biometric & Environmental History**: 24h/7d charts for temperature and humidity.
  - **Appliance Performance**: Tracking vacuum maintenance and usage patterns.

